<title>USA: Delta Air Lines names Atlantic/Pacific VP.</title>
<headline>Delta Air Lines names Atlantic/Pacific VP.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Delta Air Lines said it has appointed Stephan Egli as vice-president of its Atlantic/Pacific business unit.</p>
<p>With effect from early July, Egli will be responsible for the carrier's transoceanic operations, including determination of overall route, alliance and product development strategy.</p>
<p>Egli, 37, formerly of Swissair since 1991 as its vice-president of network management, is replacing Michael Medlicott, who resigned to take a position as managing director with Opus Holdings Plc.</p>
<p>-Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax+5017</p>
